              "fullDescription": {
                "markdown": "### Impact\nIf an application method handler crashes, the error message is included in the status message sent to the client. This can leak to the client any sensitive data that may be included in the error message. This impacts anyone using `@grpc/grpc-js` to run servers.\n\n### Patches\nThis vulnerability is fixed in 1.13.6 and 1.14.5.\n\n### Workarounds\nThis can be avoided by using a top-level error handler in method handlers to strip out sensitive error information.",
                "text": "### Impact\nIf an application method handler crashes, the error message is included in the status message sent to the client. This can leak to the client any sensitive data that may be included in the error message. This impacts anyone using `@grpc/grpc-js` to run servers.\n\n### Patches\nThis vulnerability is fixed in 1.13.6 and 1.14.5.\n\n### Workarounds\nThis can be avoided by using a top-level error handler in method handlers to strip out sensitive error information."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [CVE-2026-101915](https://osv.dev/CVE-2026-101915)**.\n\n## [GHSA-f596-whhp-79r4](https://osv.dev/GHSA-f596-whhp-79r4)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ### Impact\n\u003e If an application method handler crashes, the error message is included in the status message sent to the client. This can leak to the client any sensitive data that may be included in the error message. This impacts anyone using `@grpc/grpc-js` to run servers.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Patches\n\u003e This vulnerability is fixed in 1.13.6 and 1.14.5.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Workarounds\n\u003e This can be avoided by using a top-level error handler in method handlers to strip out sensitive error information.\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/pnpm-lock.yaml | @grpc/grpc-js | 1.14.4 |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/pnpm-lock.yaml | @grpc/grpc-js | 1.14.4 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-f596-whhp-79r4 | @grpc/grpc-js | 1.13.6, 1.14.5 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-101915\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-101915\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n",
                "text": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [CVE-2026-101915](https://osv.dev/CVE-2026-101915)**.\n\n## [GHSA-f596-whhp-79r4](https://osv.dev/GHSA-f596-whhp-79r4)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ### Impact\n\u003e If an application method handler crashes, the error message is included in the status message sent to the client. This can leak to the client any sensitive data that may be included in the error message. This impacts anyone using `@grpc/grpc-js` to run servers.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Patches\n\u003e This vulnerability is fixed in 1.13.6 and 1.14.5.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Workarounds\n\u003e This can be avoided by using a top-level error handler in method handlers to strip out sensitive error information.\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/pnpm-lock.yaml | @grpc/grpc-js | 1.14.4 |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/pnpm-lock.yaml | @grpc/grpc-js | 1.14.4 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-f596-whhp-79r4 | @grpc/grpc-js | 1.13.6, 1.14.5 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/home/runner/work/empathy/empathy/egolint/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-101915\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n`/home/runner/work/e